{"name":"Batu Cave","hex":"#595438","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"batu","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The drug methamphetamine hydrochloride, crystal meth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/batu"},{"term":"cave","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, naturally-occurring cavity formed underground or in the face of a cliff or a hillside.","A hole, depression, or gap in earth or rock, whether natural or man-made."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To surrender.","To collapse."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cave"}],"entries":[{"title":"Batu Caves","blocks":[{"text":"Batu Caves are a series of limestone caves in Gombak, Selangor, Malaysia. It is located on a 325 m (1,066 ft)–tall mogote, about 13 km (8.1 mi) north of the Malaysian capital of Kuala Lumpur. The cave complex contains many Hindu temples, the most popular of which is a shrine dedicated to Murugan, and is the focal point of the Tamil Hindu festival of Thaipusam in Malaysia. The complex hosts a 43 m (141 ft) tall Murugan statue, amongst the tallest Murugan statues in the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Batu_Caves_stairs_2022-05.jpg/330px-Batu_Caves_stairs_2022-05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batu_Caves"},{"title":"Cave","blocks":[{"text":"Caves and caverns are natural voids under the surface of the Earth and have also been observed in other rocky worlds. Caves often form by the weathering of rock and can extend deep underground. Exogene caves are smaller openings that extend a relatively short distance underground. Caves which extend farther underground than the opening is wide are called endogene caves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Lechuguilla_Cave_Pearlsian_Gulf.jpg/330px-Lechuguilla_Cave_Pearlsian_Gulf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&ut